    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d688">

                <pb facs="0687" n="571" xml:id="pg571"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 365.117/113.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador Page</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 188.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 29, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your telegram No. 332 of
                    June 18, 1915, concerning the detention of Enrico Ajello for military service,
                    the Department sends you herewith copy of a letter<anchor n="5" xml:id="d688-f1"
                    /> of July 14, 1915, from Mr. Elmer C. Miller, asking that representations be
                    made to the Italian Government for the release of Mr. Ajello. It is desired that
                    you request an early decision of this case, and to report the result.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
